---
import GovLayout from '../../layouts/GovLayout.astro';
import PhaseBanner from '../../components/PhaseBanner.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import SummaryBox from '../../components/SummaryBox.astro';
import InsetText from '../../components/InsetText.astro';
import Sidebar from '../../components/Sidebar.astro';
---
<GovLayout title="Arrest & Wanted System" department="Ministry of Justice" description="How the Wanted status, arrest mechanics, confiscation, and police progression work in ASEAN Motor Club.">

<PhaseBanner tag="Policy" text="Updated 8 April 2026" />
<Breadcrumbs items={[
  { label: "Justice & Law Enforcement", href: "/justice" },
  { label: "Arrest & Wanted System", href: "/justice/arrest-wanted" },
]} />

<main class="govuk-main-wrapper">
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <h1>Arrest &amp; Wanted System</h1>

      <SummaryBox title="Summary">
        <p>Delivering illicit cargo creates a <strong>Criminal Record</strong> (the <code>[C]</code> tag). A Wanted status may additionally apply. On arrest, police confiscate your <strong>Wanted bounty plus your confiscatable amount</strong>, and your Criminal Record is cleared. Police may also manually flag suspects using <code>/setwanted</code>, subject to a 1-hour cooldown after prior Wanted expiry. <strong>Teleporting while Wanted triggers an automatic arrest.</strong></p>
      </SummaryBox>

      <h2 id="criminal-record">1. Criminal Record</h2>
      <p>Your first illicit delivery creates an active <strong>Criminal Record</strong>, applies the <code>[C]</code> tag to your name, and begins accumulating two amounts:</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Criminal Record fields</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>amount</strong></td>
            <td>Permanent lifetime total of all illicit delivery payments on this record. Used for criminal level display.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>confiscatable_amount</strong></td>
            <td>Also accumulates with deliveries but <strong>decays with a 2-hour half-life while online</strong>. This is what is seized on arrest. Sorted and displayed in <code>/wanted</code>.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>The Criminal Record is <strong>never cleared by time</strong>. It is only cleared on arrest, which immediately removes the <code>[C]</code> tag.</p>

      <InsetText>
        Only one active Criminal Record can exist per character at a time. A new record is created fresh after each arrest.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="wanted-status">2. Wanted Status</h2>
      <p>Deliveries above a value threshold may trigger an additional <strong>Wanted</strong> status on top of the Criminal Record. The probability scales with delivery value — from a <strong>10% floor</strong> on any amount up to <strong>100%</strong> for deliveries worth <strong>$100,000 or more</strong>. Any Wanted status (new or refreshed) is subject to a <strong>minimum bounty of $50,000</strong>. A Wanted status can also be manually applied by on-duty police via <code>/setwanted</code>.</p>

      <InsetText>
        <strong>30-second debounce window:</strong> Multiple deliveries within 30 seconds of each other are aggregated before the probability roll. Splitting large cargo into many small deliveries is treated as a single delivery of the combined value.
      </InsetText>

      <h3>Time-limited status — proximity slows decay</h3>
      <p>Wanted heat decays at a <strong>constant rate of 1.0 heat/second</strong> when no police are nearby. A full W5 status (300 heat) expires naturally in <strong>5 minutes</strong> if you avoid all police.</p>
      <p>When an on-duty officer is within <strong>200 m</strong>, the server <em>reduces</em> the decay rate proportional to their proximity (1/r² law). Getting close to a cop makes the timer run slower; staying far away lets it expire at full speed. Decay never reverses — heat only ever decreases.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Effective decay rate per second by distance to nearest officer</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>Decay rate/s</th><th>Time to expire (from W5)</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>10 m (point-blank)</td><td>~0.09</td><td>~55 minutes</td><td>Decay very slow</td></tr>
          <tr><td>50 m</td><td>~0.17</td><td>~30 minutes</td><td>Decay slow</td></tr>
          <tr><td>100 m <em>(reference)</em></td><td>0.5</td><td>10 minutes</td><td>Decay halved</td></tr>
          <tr><td>150 m</td><td>~0.69</td><td>~7.2 minutes</td><td>Decay reduced</td></tr>
          <tr><td>≥200 m (escape gate)</td><td>1.0</td><td>5 minutes</td><td>Full decay, can expire</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No police / offline</td><td>1.0</td><td>5 minutes</td><td>Full decay</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <InsetText>
        Wanted cannot expire while any officer is within 200 m — heat is clamped at a W1 floor. Once all officers are beyond 200 m, the floor lifts and natural decay brings it to zero automatically.
      </InsetText>

      <h3>Star indicator (W1–W5)</h3>
      <p>Your Wanted severity is displayed as a star level from W1 to W5. All Wanted statuses begin at <strong>W5 (maximum heat, 300 heat units)</strong>. Stars are based on remaining heat with each band covering 60 units:</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Star level by remaining heat</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Stars</th><th>Remaining heat</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">W5 (max)</td><td>241 – 300</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">W4</td><td>181 – 240</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">W3</td><td>121 – 180</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">W2</td><td>61 – 120</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">W1</td><td>1 – 60</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">Expired</td><td>0</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>You receive an in-game system message each time your star level changes. When fully expired, you are notified and a server-wide announcement confirms your escape.</p>

      <h3>Auto-arrest on teleport</h3>
      <p>Teleporting while Wanted is considered a direct attempt to evade capture. The following actions trigger an <strong>immediate automatic arrest</strong> (teleport to jail and full confiscation):</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Teleporting:</strong> Any manual teleport (via <code>/tp</code>, menu, or portals) while Wanted results in immediate arrest.</li>
        <li><strong>Vehicle Reset:</strong> Using roadside recovery (Rescue) while Wanted results in immediate arrest.</li>
        <li><strong>Respawning:</strong> Respawning at a hospital or garage while Wanted results in immediate arrest.</li>
        <li><strong>Logging out:</strong> Your Wanted status persists and resumes when you log back in. If you log back in near police, heat may escalate, but you are not arrested until you teleport or are captured.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="setwanted">3. Manual Wanted — <code>/setwanted</code></h2>
      <p>On-duty police officers can manually flag a player as Wanted using <code>/setwanted &lt;name&gt;</code>. The command:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Requires the officer to be on duty</li>
        <li>Requires the target to be online</li>
        <li>Cannot be used on yourself or on a player who is already Wanted</li>
        <li>Displays a warning note if the target has no active Criminal Record (possibly innocent)</li>
        <li>Is subject to a <strong>1-hour cooldown</strong> from the target's last Wanted expiry — officers cannot immediately re-target a recently released player</li>
      </ul>

      <InsetText>
        The cooldown reply shows the exact remaining minutes: "You can set them as wanted again in <em>N</em> minute(s)."
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="arrest-zones">4. Arrest Zones</h2>
      <p>Arrests can only be initiated when the <strong>Police officer is inside a designated Arrest Zone</strong>. These are geographic polygons defined by government administrators. If no active arrest zones exist, the zone check is bypassed and arrests can occur anywhere.</p>

      <h2 id="police-conduct">5. Police Conduct &amp; Arrest Procedure</h2>
      <p>Police officers must follow the correct procedure before initiating an arrest. Skipping steps or targeting ineligible players is considered misconduct.</p>

      <h3>Who may be arrested</h3>
      <p>Officers may <strong>only target players with an active Criminal (<code>[C]</code>) tag</strong> — either displayed in-game or confirmed as Wanted via the system. Players without a Criminal Record may not be stopped or arrested.</p>

      <h3>Required procedure</h3>
      <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li><strong>Signal the suspect to stop and pull over.</strong> Use lights, sirens, or in-game voice/chat to make the request clear.</li>
        <li><strong>Allow a reasonable opportunity to comply.</strong> Give the suspect time to react before beginning a pursuit.</li>
        <li><strong>Only pursue and arrest uncooperative suspects.</strong> If the suspect pulls over and complies, engage through roleplay — not immediate arrest. Arrests are reserved for suspects who flee or refuse to stop.</li>
      </ol>

      <InsetText>
        Failure to follow this procedure — such as instantly arresting a compliant suspect — may result in a roleplay violation. The auto-arrest system enforces proximity rules but cannot enforce conduct; officer discretion is expected.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="manual-arrest">6. Manual Arrest (<code>/arrest</code>)</h2>
      <p>On-duty Police officers can initiate a manual arrest using the <code>/arrest</code> command. The process takes <strong>3 seconds</strong> to complete.</p>

      <h3>Eligibility requirements</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Officer must have an <strong>active Police session</strong> (on duty)</li>
        <li>Officer must be within an <strong>active Arrest Zone</strong> (if any zones are configured)</li>
        <li>Officer must <strong>not have teleported recently</strong> (5-minute cooldown after teleporting)</li>
        <li>Officer must not currently be Wanted themselves</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Arrest radius</h3>
      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Arrest range by officer state</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Officer state</th><th>Arrest radius</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>On foot</td><td>30 metres</td></tr>
          <tr><td>In a police vehicle</td><td>20 metres</td></tr>
          <tr><td>In a civilian vehicle</td><td>Cannot arrest</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>Verification polling</h3>
      <p>Once <code>/arrest</code> is initiated, the system polls positions <strong>every second for 3 seconds</strong>. During this window:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>The <strong>officer must stay within arrest range</strong> of each suspect</li>
        <li>Suspects must remain <strong>below ~20 km/h</strong>. Suspects moving faster are dropped from the arrest</li>
        <li>Suspects who go offline are dropped from the arrest</li>
      </ul>
      <p>After 3 successful polls, the arrest is executed on all remaining targets.</p>

      <h2 id="auto-arrest">7. Auto-Arrest Patrol</h2>
      <p>The auto-arrest system runs continuously, monitoring on-duty officers and nearby suspects. When a Wanted suspect remains within range and below the speed limit for long enough, the arrest fires automatically — no officer command required.</p>

      <h3>Parameters</h3>
      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Auto-arrest parameters</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Poll interval</td><td>Every 0.5 seconds</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Time until arrest</td><td>4 seconds (8 consecutive ticks)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Warning issued after</td><td>1.5 seconds (3rd tick)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>On-foot arrest radius</td><td>40 metres (checked on first contact only)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>In-vehicle arrest radius</td><td>12 metres (checked on first contact only)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Suspect speed limit</td><td>30 km/h</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>Process</h3>
      <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li>The patrol loop identifies all on-duty officers and all non-police players online.</li>
        <li>For each officer, it checks whether they are on foot or in a <strong>police vehicle</strong> (vehicle name must contain "Police"). Officers in civilian vehicles cannot auto-arrest.</li>
        <li>Officers within active Arrest Zones (if configured) scan for nearby Wanted suspects within range.</li>
        <li>When a Wanted suspect is first detected within range, a <strong>stillness counter</strong> begins for that cop–suspect pair.</li>
        <li>If the suspect moves faster than 30 km/h, the counter resets.</li>
        <li>At the <strong>3rd tick (1.5 seconds)</strong>, the suspect receives a warning: <em>"A police officer is attempting to arrest you! Flee now!"</em></li>
        <li>At the <strong>8th tick (4 seconds)</strong>, the arrest is executed automatically.</li>
      </ol>

      <InsetText>
        The auto-arrest radius (40 m on foot) is larger than the manual arrest radius (30 m), but suspects have more time to react — 4 seconds vs 3 seconds. Keeping moving above 30 km/h resets the counter.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="confiscation">8. Confiscation</h2>
      <p>On arrest, <strong>two amounts</strong> are confiscated simultaneously:</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>What is confiscated on arrest</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Active Wanted bounty</td>
            <td><code>Wanted.amount</code> — starts at delivery value (floored at $50,000), grows during police chases</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Criminal Record confiscatable amount</td>
            <td><code>CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</code> — decays over time while online</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p><strong>Total confiscation = Wanted.amount + CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</strong></p>

      <InsetText>
        There is no partial confiscation based on star level. If you are arrested at W1 or W5, the same full combined amount is seized.
      </InsetText>

      <h3>Bounty growth during police chases</h3>
      <p>While you are Wanted and police officers are within 200 m, your Wanted bounty increases each tick using the same 1/r² proximity law as decay reduction (closer = faster growth). Bounty is separate from heat — it accumulates permanently and is the amount seized on arrest:</p>
      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Bounty growth rate by proximity to nearest officer</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>Growth rate</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>10 m (point-blank)</td><td>+$500/s</td></tr>
          <tr><td>50 m</td><td>+$200/s</td></tr>
          <tr><td>100 m <em>(reference)</em></td><td>+$50/s</td></tr>
          <tr><td>≥200 m (escape gate)</td><td>+$0/s</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>The Wanted bounty resets to zero when the Wanted status expires (escape). However, your Criminal Record and its confiscatable amount remain — a future arrest will still seize that amount.</p>

      <h3>What happens to confiscated money</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Deducted from the suspect's wallet</strong> via the mod server</li>
        <li><strong>Recorded as Treasury income</strong> under "Police Confiscation"</li>
        <li><strong>The suspect's criminal laundered total is reduced</strong> by the confiscated Criminal Record amount</li>
        <li><strong>The arresting officer receives the full confiscated amount</strong> as a reward — both as in-game money and wallet credit</li>
        <li>A <strong>Confiscation record</strong> is permanently created, linking the suspect, officer, and amount</li>
        <li>The <strong>Criminal Record is cleared</strong> and the <code>[C]</code> tag is immediately removed</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>No Wanted = arrest still possible</h3>
      <p>If a player has an active Criminal Record (<code>[C]</code> tag) but no active Wanted status, they can still be arrested (teleported to jail and Criminal Record cleared). Only the <code>confiscatable_amount</code> is seized — there is no Wanted bounty to confiscate.</p>

      <h2 id="jail-containment">9. Jail Containment</h2>
      <p>When a player is arrested — whether by manual <code>/arrest</code>, auto-arrest patrol, or any other arrest path — they are immediately teleported to the designated <strong>Jail</strong> location. A <strong>30-second boundary enforcement</strong> period then begins automatically.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Jail containment parameters</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Boundary radius</td><td>10 metres from the jail marker</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Enforcement duration</td><td>30 seconds after arrest</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Check frequency</td><td>Every second</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Teleport on escape</td><td>Immediate — vehicles are despawned</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>During the 30-second window, if the player moves more than <strong>10 metres</strong> from the jail marker, the server <strong>instantly teleports them back</strong> and shows a warning popup. This repeats on every tick until the containment period expires.</p>

      <InsetText>
        After 30 seconds the containment ends automatically and the player is free to move. There is no manual release step — the timer is enforced server-side and cannot be shortened.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="security-bonus">10. Security Risk Bonus</h2>
      <p>When active police officers are online, illicit delivery payments are increased to reflect the higher risk. Each on-duty officer adds <strong>50% to the base payout</strong>, capped at <strong>+250%</strong> (with 5 or more officers).</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Risk bonus by number of active officers</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Active officers</th><th>Bonus on delivery</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">0</td><td>+0%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">1</td><td>+50%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">2</td><td>+100%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">3</td><td>+150%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">4</td><td>+200%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">5+</td><td>+250% (maximum)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="police-progression">11. Police Progression</h2>
      <p>Officers advance in level based on their cumulative confiscated amount. Every <strong>$50,000 confiscated</strong> increases the officer's level by 1. When an officer levels up, their player tag is refreshed and a server-wide announcement is broadcast.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Police level thresholds</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Cumulative confiscated</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">1</td><td>$0 – $49,999</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">2</td><td>$50,000 – $99,999</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">3</td><td>$100,000 – $149,999</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left"><em>N</em></td><td><em>(N − 1) × $50,000</em> onwards</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="smuggling-tipoff">12. Smuggling Tip-Offs</h2>
      <p>When a player loads illicit cargo, the system may broadcast a server-wide tip-off: <em>"Intelligence reports suggest a smuggling operation is underway"</em>. This is controlled by the <code>SMUGGLING_TIPOFF_ENABLED</code> server setting.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Tip-off parameters</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Delay before broadcast</td><td>15 seconds</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cooldown per player</td><td>60 seconds</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <InsetText>
        Tip-offs do not reveal the player's name or location — they only alert police that a smuggling operation is in progress.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="modded-vehicles">13. Modded Vehicle Rules</h2>
      <p>Players using vehicles with custom-modified parts face additional penalties during illicit cargo gameplay:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>On delivery:</strong> Criminal profits are zeroed out (transferred back as a penalty) if modded parts are detected on the player's active vehicle.</li>
        <li><strong>On load:</strong> A warning popup is shown: "You are not allowed to use modified vehicles for criminal gameplay."</li>
        <li><strong>Police exception:</strong> On-duty officers with police-issued whitelisted parts are exempt from modded vehicle detection.</li>
      </ul>

    </div>
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-one-third">
      <Sidebar items={[
        { label: "Criminal Record", href: "#criminal-record" },
        { label: "Wanted Status", href: "#wanted-status" },
        { label: "/setwanted", href: "#setwanted" },
        { label: "Arrest Zones", href: "#arrest-zones" },
        { label: "Police Conduct", href: "#police-conduct" },
        { label: "Manual Arrest", href: "#manual-arrest" },
        { label: "Auto-Arrest Patrol", href: "#auto-arrest" },
        { label: "Confiscation", href: "#confiscation" },
        { label: "Jail Containment", href: "#jail-containment" },
        { label: "Security Risk Bonus", href: "#security-bonus" },
        { label: "Police Progression", href: "#police-progression" },
        { label: "Smuggling Tip-Offs", href: "#smuggling-tipoff" },
        { label: "Modded Vehicle Rules", href: "#modded-vehicles" },
      ]} />
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

</GovLayout>
